j=base('launch_double_circulation_routes','Double circulation: engineer the route','Trace a blood journey, test a valve and calculate a pump output','Explain how heart structure supports double circulation and calculate cardiac output from supplied data.',4,'Directly develops C32 through Pearson 8.7, 8.8 and 8.12. This LAUNCH exemplar adds named chambers, major vessels, pressure reasoning and calculations; it does not claim a wholly untouched topic or complete cardiovascular teaching.',['Blood carries materials between organs.','Lungs exchange oxygen and carbon dioxide with blood.','A rate includes an amount and a time.'],['Trace the body–heart–lungs–heart–body route with named chambers and vessels.','Explain valves and the thicker left-ventricle wall using function.','Calculate output with correct units and state a limitation of the constructed data.'],[('artery','A vessel carrying blood away from the heart.'),('vein','A vessel carrying blood towards the heart.'),('atrium','A heart chamber that receives returning blood.'),('ventricle','A heart chamber that pumps blood out of the heart.'),('stroke volume','The volume pumped by a ventricle in one beat.'),('cardiac output','The volume pumped by a ventricle per minute: stroke volume multiplied by heart rate.')])
