j['misconceptions']=[misconception('An artery is defined as carrying oxygen-rich blood.','Arteries carry blood away from the heart; the pulmonary artery carries oxygen-poor blood to the lungs.','Ask what makes the pulmonary artery an artery.'),misconception('The left ventricle pumps more blood per beat because its wall is thicker.','In steady circulation the two sides have matching average outputs; the thicker wall generates the higher pressure needed for the systemic route.','Separate pressure from volume in the explanation.'),misconception('Valves actively pump the blood.','Muscle contraction creates pressure; valves open/close with pressure differences to prevent backflow.','Ask which structure supplies the pushing action.'),misconception('A fast heart rate alone proves greater output.','Stroke volume matters too; output is the product of the two quantities.','Compare both columns before judging a pump record.')]
